# state: any   (the golden cc9b4ced4a0f holds pathfind's profile; lane.accuracy804, #804)
# RalliSport Challenge (4D53000F): rallisport-804c.route (pathfind's Single Race path, hat released
# at once) with the race shots back to back. 804c's capture (1791150087-lane.accuracy804-2199171)
# reached the race and its dump records the near rival's body in every frame from race clock ~8
# to ~10; it had no images, so it cannot say whether that run flickered. Sixteen screencaps with
# no wait between them (0.7-2.4 s each on 804c's log) from race clock ~5.6 cover the rival pass:
# with the body absent on alternate frames, several of them show the shadow without the body.
# Every press keeps 804c's measured time (start-race A +140.6, race clock 0 ~+147.4).
wait 20
shot boot20
wait 20
shot boot40
wait 20
mark booted
press START
wait 5
shot title
wait 3
press A
wait 6
press A
wait 6
shot mainmenu
# RIGHT exactly as pathfind sends it (pathfind.py send(): HATX max, HATX mid at once, then 0.35 s).
# 804b held the hat 0.35 s between max and mid: the menu auto-repeated past Single Race to Options.
axis HATX max
axis HATX mid
wait 2.35
press A
wait 6
shot racetype
press A
wait 6
shot track
press A
wait 6
shot car
press A
wait 25
shot options
press A
wait 8
press A
wait 3
shot r1
shot r2
shot r3
shot r4
shot r5
shot r6
shot r7
shot r8
shot r9
shot r10
shot r11
shot r12
shot r13
shot r14
shot r15
shot r16
mark gameplay
repeat forever {
    wait 20
    shot hold
}
